WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.398 --> 00:00:03.065
(calming music)

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.715
- The first time I really
took a horse in the water,

00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:41.924
I had a friend that had
horses on the north coast.

00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:44.674
Her house was right on the beach.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:47.898
We set up some little jumps and we were

00:00:47.898 --> 00:00:49.705
going over with her horse.

00:00:49.705 --> 00:00:51.097
And she said, "Oh, it's too hot.

00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:51.930
It's too hot.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:55.430
We've got to take the horse in the water."

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:58.618
I said, "We can't take the horse in the,

00:00:58.618 --> 00:01:01.106
in the sea like that."

00:01:01.106 --> 00:01:02.319
She said, "Yeah, sure.

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:03.889
Come on, jump on."

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:06.556
(calming music)

00:01:11.855 --> 00:01:13.310
You know, the waves were coming in

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.351
and the horse just sort of lifted his head

00:01:15.351 --> 00:01:18.340
and the waves would come over.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.775
And we just went in a little bit deeper

00:01:19.775 --> 00:01:23.025
and a little bit deeper and
then he started swimming.

00:01:23.025 --> 00:01:25.692
(calming music)

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:44.207
You can ride all your life

00:01:44.207 --> 00:01:46.938
and you've never felt that smoothness,

00:01:46.938 --> 00:01:49.923
that, that power but with no uh,

00:01:49.923 --> 00:01:52.115
there was no jolt at all.

00:01:52.115 --> 00:01:54.447
It was just so absolutely like silk.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.114
(calming music)

